Assignment 5 – GitHub Repository Link

Introduction

GitHub is a platform used to store and manage project files online. It helps developers save and share their work.

Steps to Create a GitHub Repository

1. Open "www.github.com" (https://github.com).
2. Log in to your GitHub account.
3. Click on New Repository.
4. Enter the repository name: "html-css-assignments".
5. Keep the repository empty and click on Create Repository.

Steps to Upload Project Files

Open your local project folder in the terminal and run these commands:

1. Add GitHub repository link

"git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/html-css-assignments.git"

2. Set the main branch

"git branch -M main"

3. Upload files to GitHub

"git push -u origin main"

After uploading, refresh the GitHub page. All project files and commits will be visible there.

Optional: Host Website for Free

1. Open your GitHub repository.
2. Go to Settings.
3. Click on Pages.
4. Select Branch: "main".
5. Select Folder: "/ (root)".
6. Click Save.

Your website will be available at:

"https://<your-username>.github.io/html-css-assignments/"

Submission

Repository Link:

"https://github.com/<your-username>/html-css-assignments"

Replace "<your-username>" with your actual GitHub username.

